{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage","id":1481989,"title":"What is your playstyle for Mage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-26T06:29:35-07:00","id":1481989,"title":"What is your playstyle for Mage?","content":"I've noticed there seems to be 2 different play-styles in the mage community and I want to see how common each is. For lack of better terms I'll call it &quot;wide&quot; and &quot;narrow&quot; play.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wide&quot; play I'm defining for this discussion as when the players and STs treat the sphere system as more open ended with a lot of overlap. For example: A wide ST could allow the Life to manipulate a person's emotions and sanity via manipulating hormones, but it would be objectively worse at it than mind(it takes life 5 to not mentally devolve into an animal if you shape-ship into one and Life 6+ to prevent the same when shapeshifting others, but the same thing can be pulled of with a rote using life 4 and the mind sphere).<ul><li>Pros: players have more freedom to come up with interesting effects and this can lead to more interesting stories.</li> <li>cons: Obviously this can get out of hand because player can easily become Much more powerful at lower sphere levels. I've played games like this where the Original end boss was killed way too early because the ST underestimated how creative his players could get.</li> </ul><br /> &quot;Narrow&quot; play I'm defining for this discussion as when players and STs remove any overlap between sphere and require multi-sphere effects for any complex effect. For example: A &quot;narrow&quot; play ST may require the time sphere as well as the life sphere for any effect that makes the mage younger, even if the effect was for creating a new body rather than reversing their own age).<ul><li>Pro: This makes it Much easier to pace and balance a story, making it possible to plan out more of the campaign.</li> <li>Cons: This can get very Rail-Roady and annoying, Especially if the ST in question thinks their interpretation is the &quot;one true canon&quot;. I've spoken with STs who've argued until they were blue in the face that the Forces sphere was required for any kind of telekinesis style effect, until I showed them the page number and references in Every mage core book from 2nd to 20th that specifically said Forces, Matter, and Correspondence could do that(Most of them then doubled down and said <i>Their</i> table require forces and continued to say by that <i>theirs</i> was &quot;the right way&quot; to rule on that).</li> </ul>There are likely a thousand other ways to look at this(some hermetic in the distance is likely ranting about paradigms as I type this), so If anyone has any other playstyle trends they've noticed feel free to bring them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T06:42:32-07:00","id":1481990,"title":"","content":"Wide. I'm a big believer that the purple Paradigm is just a way to represent the system of the game. Not the valid way all things have to break down into.<br /> <br /> To summarize, I read on SV from earthscorpion,that the purple paradigm is basically treating the rules of the game as the way the setting &quot;really&quot; works. M20 is very much written from this perspective - the version I prefer to run, which is Revised-era, very much doesn't.<br /> <br /> Under the purple paradigm, when you throw a fireball at someone, you're using Forces 3 to make a fireball and justifying it with invocations of the angel Gabriel. Under the version I uses, there is a person who can invoke the angel Gabriel to call heavenly fire down on someone, and this is represented in the game mechanics by them having &quot;Forces 3&quot; on their character sheet. Mostly only Hermetics talk about the Nine Great Spheres (and people trying to use the Traditions' magical Esperanto to work out how to get their ritual working and get their paradigms working together).<br /> <br /> Hence, under the purple paradigm, Traditionalists basically know all along that they're using their Avatar to warp reality and then justifying it with whatever they believe in. This has the major problem that it means that any historical figure who was a mage didn't really believe in their ideas, and just hid the truth from the Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Rejecting the purple paradigm, however, means that Newton could do various alchemical acts, forms of advanced mathematics which let him predict things, and magical things involving light using lenses and crystals. This is represented by him having Matter 4, Forces 3, Time 2, etc on his character sheet, but he probably didn't think about it this way. He could just do these things because he'd studied them. His mathematics and optics would be accepted into the later Consensus and so he's respected for them, but his belief in alchemy is laughed at and used as an example of how even figures as influential as he was can be wrong about things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","user":"Vendrin","date":". 05-26-2022, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T06:46:25-07:00","id":1481993,"title":"","content":"I prefer the wide approach. My go-to approach for reining in abuse is to insist on more successes if you don't have the \u201cright\u201d Spheres for an Effect; though that's more of a guideline than a rule. Basically, if the player's explanation for why his choice of Spheres makes sense to me (whether or not it matches the rules as written), I assign the usual number of required successes for the task (two, by default); if it feels a bit off, I might allow it but call for twice as many successes. That <i>usually</i> means that the Effect is going to require a ritual, as there aren't many mages with sufficient Arete to reliably achieve 4+ successes on a single roll; so in practice, this leans a bit into the \u201cnarrow play\u201d in that there's some disincentive to use non-standard sphere choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T12:31:22-07:00","id":1482017,"title":"","content":"Middle?<br /> <br /> I mean, I would generally approach thing as &quot;wide,&quot; but not beyond the scope laid out in the books. You can use Life to mess with people's hormones... the books even tell you what that does. I'm not going to let Life go beyond that; the edges between the Spheres should be plenty blurry, but there should also be some clear areas where something is under a given Sphere and not in the hazy middle between it and the others. I've also always been a strong proponent of the PBD approach, which means multi-Sphere requirements is a natural to my playstyle.<br /> <br /> Getting too &quot;wide&quot; makes the game impossible to run, and too &quot;narrow&quot; makes the game too restrictive to enjoy.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should just call my style the &quot;Awakening&quot; style, because I think Awakening 2e hit it out of the park with finally managing to make Mage magic work as a game tool in a fashion Ascension has so far never really done, even if Ascension will continue to be one of my favorite lore/setting things of all time. It makes sure each Arcanum is good enough as a self-contained power to be fun for &quot;wide&quot; magic, but the general rules ensure that there's far greater consistency in what does what that appeals more to the &quot;narrow&quot; approach's advantages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vendrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1481990#post1481990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To summarize, I read on SV from earthscorpion,that the purple paradigm is basically treating the rules of the game as the way the setting &quot;really&quot; works.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;purple paradigm,&quot; lost all meaning decades ago (aka before M20 even came out) because it's Internet mage-flamewar lingo that means completely different things to completely different people and doesn't really express anything helpful (and I'm not sure it ever did, even going back to the old Mage BBS flamewars about it).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> M20 is very much written from this perspective - the version I prefer to run, which is Revised-era, very much doesn't. </div> </div> </div>For example, that's what the 2e fans said about Revised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Under the purple paradigm, when you throw a fireball at someone, you're using Forces 3 to make a fireball and justifying it with invocations of the angel Gabriel. Under the version I uses, there is a person who can invoke the angel Gabriel to call heavenly fire down on someone, and this is represented in the game mechanics by them having &quot;Forces 3&quot; on their character sheet. </div> </div> </div>They're the same thing. That's the whole point of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mostly only Hermetics talk about the Nine Great Spheres (and people trying to use the Traditions' magical Esperanto to work out how to get their ritual working and get their paradigms working together). </div> </div> </div>Funny, the Revised Tradition books all have extensive passages on how each of the Traditions views the Spheres, as nine of them (and frequently what they think the 10th one really is). Seems like after generations of the Traditions exchanging in magical knowledge that it's been generations since any of the Traditions didn't think of things in terms of there being nine Spheres one masters to master magic. The Hermetics aren't the only occult academics in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hence, under the purple paradigm, Traditionalists basically know all along that they're using their Avatar to warp reality and then justifying it with whatever they believe in. This has the major problem that it means that any historical figure who was a mage didn't really believe in their ideas, and just hid the truth from the Sleepers. </div> </div> </div>Except, as M20 is better at stressing than Revised: the mage actually needs to believe it too. They might have intellectually figured out that in theory magic doesn't depend on belief and that a mage could learn how to shed their beliefs and just change things how they want. But none of them know how, because they still need to believe in their magical training and style to do magic even if they know it should be possible without that. What you're calling the &quot;purple paradigm,&quot; is what the Traditions call &quot;Ascension.&quot; A state they want to find but haven't figure out yet.<br /> <br /> You don't need to &quot;reject&quot; anything to make some historical figure a mage if you feel like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T12:59:16-07:00","id":1482020,"title":"","content":"I would only point out that the so-called \u201cpurple paradigm\u201d (which I'd define as something like \u201cit's all the same, even when it isn't\u201d) is very nearly unique to the Traditions. The idea that your magical theories and practice are something that can and should be discarded is <i>not</i> something you'll hear the Technocracy or the Crafts subscribing to. It's basically what holds the Traditions together, and what sets them apart from everyone else. <br /> <br /> But I really don't see what that has to do with a Wide or Narrow playstyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T13:44:16-07:00","id":1482024,"title":"","content":"I've seen some interpretations of the &quot;purple paradigm&quot; used to both promote or disparage the more extreme &quot;wide&quot; take on things depending on the poster's feelings about it. There are certainly some people that like to take &quot;wide&quot; as far as possible to the point where considerations like belief and paradigm don't really factor into play and it's just willworkers going gonzo on the setting.with only how much they can convince their ST of what their current Spheres can do as a control.. and people that think playing like that is horrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T20:25:34-07:00","id":1482048,"title":"","content":"Middle. I honestly dont care much about what the books say, because the books say a ton of nonsense that I dont agree with and that contradicts itself ALL THE TIME.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I stick to the principles:<br /> - the mage paradigm;<br /> - number of successes required<br /> And<br /> - the STRICT descrition of what the Spheres allow (NOT the examples).<br /> <br /> So, Life 3 is &quot;minor&quot; changes or &quot;simple&quot; life? (My house rule: &quot;simple&quot; here is everything from FISHES bellow. Vertebrates from anfibious above is &quot;complex). So that's what you got.<br /> <br /> In that regard for example, I always HATED the description of Forces, because it conflicts with my first and third principle. &quot;Minor&quot; and &quot;bigger&quot; forces makes no sense. The difference between a breeze and a hurricane should NOT be between Forces 3 and 5, but rather betwern 1 success or 10. Isnt it stated that &quot;the power of the effect depend on the number of successes&quot;? Well, when I use Mind 3 Im walking in Dreams, but Mind 5 is not &quot;walk in even more dreams&quot;... Mind 5 does something entirely different that cannot be done with Mind 3, is not just simply a &quot;stronger Mind 3&quot;. Just like Entropy 4 is NOT &quot;control all the dices' rolls of the entire cassino&quot;. NO! It's an entirely different capacity that is not already present in a weaker form in Entropy 2.<br /> <br /> So I changed that, Forces 2 and 3 now deal with kinetic, electromagnetism and heat, and Forces 4 and 5 deal with Nuclear and Gravity (and my 6 deals with &quot;weird&quot; forces). <br /> <br /> That being said, whatever effect you wanna do, check what your Spheres levels allow you to do. If it's there, I dont care about the fluff, as long as the fluff isnt directly contrary to the effect or to the Paradigm. Do you believe that when you pray to make your computer faster, you are actually summoning the spirits of computational speed to help? Ok, are you using Entropy 3 for that? What does Entropy 3 says? &quot;Affect Matter&quot;. Ok, done. No, there is NO need to use Spirit. The &quot;speed by Spirits&quot; is fluff, NOT game mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T20:58:47-07:00","id":1482051,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, my understanding is that the reason why Forces are the way they are in M20 has to do with a quirk in the magic system: the higher the Sphere requirement for the Effect, the fewer successes you're likely to get. That means that if you try to create a hurricane, you'll be better off using Forces 3 to do it than Forces 5: Forces 3 is Difficulty 8, while Forces 5 is Difficulty 10. And because the final Difficulty can't be reduced more than -3, the best you can do is Difficulty 5 vs. Difficulty 7. <br /> <br /> Personally, I ignore that cap; I <i>want</i> my players loading up on the negative Magical Modifiers, to a minimum of Difficulty 3; so that means that the higher Difficulty of Forces 5 translates to more effort put into making the Effect\u2026 effective, rather than on the dice pool being less effective","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T01:19:11-07:00","id":1482229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482051#post1482051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, my understanding is that the reason why Forces are the way they are in M20 has to do with a quirk in the magic system: the higher the Sphere requirement for the Effect, the fewer successes you're likely to get. That means that if you try to create a hurricane, you'll be better off using Forces 3 to do it than Forces 5: Forces 3 is Difficulty 8, while Forces 5 is Difficulty 10. And because the final Difficulty can't be reduced more than -3, the best you can do is Difficulty 5 vs. Difficulty 7. <br /> <br /> Personally, I ignore that cap; I <i>want</i> my players loading up on the negative Magical Modifiers, to a minimum of Difficulty 3; so that means that the higher Difficulty of Forces 5 translates to more effort put into making the Effect\u2026 effective, rather than on the dice pool being less effective</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Even so, that doesnt come as a problem for any other Spheres. Is that because Forces is the &quot;fireball&quot; damage Sphere? Wanting Forces just because it gives +1 damage is silly. Besides, damage is, once again, successes driven, so you're still better of using Forces 3 - heck, no, Forces 2.<br /> <br /> I always both had and helped my players be creative thou. One of the best damage dealers we had came from my route &quot;Octopodes&quot;, which used only Life 2 to create &quot;killer squids&quot; able to breath air and walk, hunting their pray using pheromones. You needed only a DNA replica - which could be &quot;determined&quot; and &quot;replicated&quot; by my vary sofisticate etherite &quot;spectrometer&quot; (blink blink) using Life 1.<br /> <br /> I intended to have those as chantry defenses, but one of my Etherite players surprised me by creating the &quot;Octo-bazooca&quot;, connecting them to a tank in a car and literalling SHOOTING those little devils filled with claws and fangs and ACID on enemies. The Octobazooca became a legendary item - and only needed Life 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T02:39:15-07:00","id":1482230,"title":"","content":"No Prime 2? That's usually a requirement when creating something from nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T04:47:41-07:00","id":1482239,"title":"","content":"Besides any issues I have with classifying cephalopods as &quot;simple&quot; life just because they're invertebrates (using biological taxonomy doesn't make sense from a mystic perspective, and treating a squid, octopus, or cuttlefish as &quot;simpler&quot; life than a hagfish doesn't make sense to biology based cladistics),,,<br /> <br /> It's also a 5-10 success feat per the chart just to create them in the first place, and then all of the pattern bleed inducing alterations going on... it feels pretty unlikely that you could make a small pack of attack land squid in a functional fashion with just Life 3/Prime 2 (or Life 2 and higher level Time for rapid cloning I guess?). It makes no sense when you can create existing terrestrial arthropod that are capable of easily incapacitating if not killing healthy adult human beings without lots of mucking about with their Patterns. Plus the extra magic to order them around (squid aren't exactly known as easily trained attack animals).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T13:24:07-07:00","id":1482285,"title":"","content":"Pondering this gave me story ideas. I started thinking of an example that illustrates how mages with completely different spheres could create very similar effects, but then I decided to keep it for myself. Generally, there is some overlap between Spirit, Correspondence and Mind where travel is concerned. Spirit is the default sphere for travelling <i>to</i> the Umbra and from layer to layer, but is less safe than Mind 4's astral travel. When it comes to travel within places in the Umbra, I would be hard pressed to deny a player with Correspondence the right to teleport within the same world or layer, having come through a friendly NPC's Spirit Gate. <br /> <br /> In one of the earlier editions, a player in my troupe found a Rote with Spirit and Matter that allowed a melee weapon to be crafted that could be used through the Gauntlet. He would travel to the Near Umbra and then put his scythe through whichever Earthbound person the character thought deserving of execution. He had taken the Twisted Apprenticeship Flaw.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T04:18:08-07:00","id":1482473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482230#post1482230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Prime 2? That's usually a requirement when creating something from nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's true. But... That also always seemed somewhat wrong to me. If we are talking about something as fickle as forces, anyway. Since, with Forces 2 you can control &quot;minor forces&quot; or &quot;lesser forces&quot;, that means you can control temperature. You DONT need Prime 2 to heat things up... At least in theory.<br /> <br /> In theory, again, you could turn light, sound, the moviment of the wind, the enviromental heat and even the electromagnetic energies from Earth's magnetic field or from ions in the atmosphere into a fireball... Or into telekinetic energy.<br /> <br /> So, I'd say that Forces would be the one Sphere that doesnt need Prime per se... Which only makes me distaste it even more because of this dreaded rule of &quot;Prime 2&quot;.<br /> <br /> Even just Forces 2, you can already control all those forces, so in theory it can already do all that.<br /> <br /> And that's just if we only consider the scientific, &quot;technocratic&quot;, interpretation of the Spheres description.<br /> <br /> Because if we go into the metaphysical (&quot;in game&quot; ) explation, that in RAW states clearly that darkness for example is NOT an &quot;abscense of light&quot; (as it is), therefore there would be NO energy to be harnessed, but rather it's just an &quot;alternative metaphysical condition of light&quot;, this means that a hermetic CAN create light in utter darkness with Forces 2 alone simply by manipulating the &quot;metaphysical light&quot;, and that Technocrats and other techies cant do it simply due to their Paradigms.<br /> <br /> That's not the case for Matter or Life (or Spiritual creation with Spirit 5), because those only manipulate what already exists, but Forces exist everywhere - even in the Void of Space, according to that idea of &quot;metaphysical contrary&quot;.<br /> <br /> Heck, even for the Techies this might hold true in the Vaccum of Space, since they believe in this &quot;technocratic nonsense&quot; of &quot;cosmic rays&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T04:42:58-07:00","id":1482479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482239#post1482239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides any issues I have with classifying cephalopods as &amp;quot;simple&amp;quot; life just because they're invertebrates (using biological taxonomy doesn't make sense from a mystic perspective, and treating a squid, octopus, or cuttlefish as &amp;quot;simpler&amp;quot; life than a hagfish doesn't make sense to biology based cladistics),,,<br /> <br /> It's also a 5-10 success feat per the chart just to create them in the first place, and then all of the pattern bleed inducing alterations going on... it feels pretty unlikely that you could make a small pack of attack land squid in a functional fashion with just Life 3/Prime 2 (or Life 2 and higher level Time for rapid cloning I guess?). It makes no sense when you can create existing terrestrial arthropod that are capable of easily incapacitating if not killing healthy adult human beings without lots of mucking about with their Patterns. Plus the extra magic to order them around (squid aren't exactly known as easily trained attack animals).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Octopodus&quot; were designed for Chantry defense by me. Their &quot;training&quot; was a simple built in effect of Life 1 - according to superstitious nonsense - or &quot;pheromone induced behavior&quot;, according to &quot;superior etherite enlightnment&quot;, that made them non agressive towards those whose pheromones had been imprinted in their biologies (Life 1 to &quot;detect and discern&quot; the &quot;good&quot; life patterns, Life 2 to introduce it in their &quot;immune system&quot;).<br /> <br /> Since they just hang around in the protected and properly sanitized environment of the Chantry (ughh, what an ugly name, I meant &quot;laboratory&quot;), they are immune to pattern bleeding.<br /> <br /> My laboratory was thus filled with those on the roofs, attached by their mucuous membranes (which they use to attach themselves to the victims for acid spraying).<br /> <br /> It were one of my players that introduced the &quot;Octo-Bazooka&quot;, by holding them in a tank in the car. Essentially, he turned the car into a &quot;portable chantry&quot;, thus keeping the little monsters from Pattern Bleeding. And having a sort of &quot;reverse vaccum cleaner&quot; attached to it to fire those into the helpless victims.<br /> <br /> And in this they are fire and forget. Pattern Bleeding doesnt matter after they are shot, since their only job is to turn certain Life Patterns into Matter Patterns by spreading acid on them. The Pattern Bleeding aint fast enough to keep them from their function (kill however you land into), and its even better that they turn into a pile of goo after their task is done. So it doesnt matter that they have &quot;unstable biochemistry&quot; out of lab conditions, because their purpose is short. And on labs, they are an efficient defense.<br /> <br /> As for successes, yes, it's no simple task, but again, they are only produced on the labs, not on the field in the open. Also, since it uses only Life 2, althought it requires many successes, it's sort of a trivial thing. Long, but trivial.<br /> <br /> In my game this became so popular among Etherites that they began to trade the monsters and also dedicated &quot;Octo-replicating Vat Tubes&quot; for other Etherites without the know-how to do it.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;simple life&quot;, well, that's... Complicated. Largely subjective in both scientific or metaphysical terms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:22:39-07:00","id":1482525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482479#post1482479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their &quot;training&quot; was a simple built in effect of Life 1 - according to superstitious nonsense - or &quot;pheromone induced behavior&quot;, according to &quot;superior etherite enlightnment&quot;, that made them non agressive towards those whose pheromones had been imprinted in their biologies (Life 1 to &quot;detect and discern&quot; the &quot;good&quot; life patterns, Life 2 to introduce it in their &quot;immune system&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, so attack squid that attack any guests that drop by if you don't cast a permanent Life affect on each squid individually first? Again, not saying this is impossible, just exceedingly impractical; esp. since they don't have noses. While cephalopods do have a sense of smell, it's a diffuse set of pores across their mantles that's designed to pick up ambient chemicals in water. Without an organ to concentrate this process, they have very limited ways to apply this. Like they can't identify different people by &quot;smell.&quot; They rely on &quot;taste&quot; for that, which they do by touching things with their limbs. If you make an acid projecting cephalopod that keys off of pheromones at a distance? It's going to start jump on, and apply acid to the closest thing they can find rather than targeting individual enemies. Or you're just adding to how much magical alterations you're applying for no practical reason (seriously, just use ants).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since they just hang around in the protected and properly sanitized environment of the Chantry (ughh, what an ugly name, I meant &quot;laboratory&quot;), they are immune to pattern bleeding. </div> </div> </div>No they aren't. They're immune to unbelief. Pattern bleeding isn't paradox. It happens whether the effects are coincidental or vulgar. Pattern bleeding happens because the original Pattern is rejecting the magical changes inflicted on it.<br /> <br /> There's a difference between &quot;we play wide,&quot; and, &quot;we think of the rules as guidelines at best.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, since it uses only Life 2, althought it requires many successes, it's sort of a trivial thing. Long, but trivial. </div> </div> </div>So... what, you're raising these animals too? Life 2 alters simple Life Patterns, it doesn't create them. Creating them takes Life 3. And again, unless you're using some sort of higher level magic, that means they have to age naturally on top of all of the costs of feeding, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my game this became so popular among Etherites that they began to trade the monsters and also dedicated &quot;Octo-replicating Vat Tubes&quot; for other Etherites without the know-how to do it. </div> </div> </div>Well, when you let a specific thing work orders of magnitude better than it should, of course it's going to be a popular tactic.<br /> <br /> If I house ruled the game so that Prime 3 unmaking instantly destroys targets with two successes and ignores the whole damage/soak/health systems, and it inherently coincidental for technology themed mages, of course every Etherite would be using it for their ray guns..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Largely subjective in both scientific or metaphysical terms </div> </div> </div>Qualitative and subjective aren't the same thing.<br /> <br /> While there's no simple quantitative way to measure complexity in an organism, there are scientifically sound qualitative ways to demonstrate that a squid is more complex than a jelly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T20:19:37-07:00","id":1482568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482525#post1482525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great, so attack squid that attack any guests that drop by if you don't cast a permanent Life affect on each squid individually first? Again, not saying this is impossible, just exceedingly impractical; esp. since they don't have noses. While cephalopods do have a sense of smell, it's a diffuse set of pores across their mantles that's designed to pick up ambient chemicals in water. Without an organ to concentrate this process, they have very limited ways to apply this. Like they can't identify different people by &amp;quot;smell.&amp;quot; They rely on &amp;quot;taste&amp;quot; for that, which they do by touching things with their limbs. If you make an acid projecting cephalopod that keys off of pheromones at a distance? It's going to start jump on, and apply acid to the closest thing they can find rather than targeting individual enemies. Or you're just adding to how much magical alterations you're applying for no practical reason (seriously, just use ants).</div> </div> </div> </div>Pfff. You Technocrats, always trying to limit TRUE SCIENCE!<br /> <br /> Science is individual inspiration, not your boring codified manuals!<br /> <br /> No wonder we Etherites left your decadent organization, and it were the best thing we did!<br /> <br /> No noses... Hey doctor Stu, can you believe this guy? He thinks our superior Octopodus need noses to feel the pheromones hahaha, see I told you the Techies would never figure out their trans-quantonic weakness, they are trying to analyse our little pets with their biology uninspired manuals hahaha just wait for when the guys at the next convention hear about this hahahaha<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No they aren't. They're immune to unbelief. Pattern bleeding isn't paradox. It happens whether the effects are coincidental or vulgar. Pattern bleeding happens because the original Pattern is rejecting the magical changes inflicted on it.<br /> <br /> There's a difference between &amp;quot;we play wide,&amp;quot; and, &amp;quot;we think of the rules as guidelines at best.&amp;quot; </div> </div> </div>So why arent Cyborgs of the techie boys constantly suffering it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So... what, you're raising these animals too? Life 2 alters simple Life Patterns, it doesn't create them. Creating them takes Life 3. And again, unless you're using some sort of higher level magic, that means they have to age naturally on top of all of the costs of feeding, and so on. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I was raising them indeed. It's not like they are difficult to capture in nature.<br /> And the Etherites have the resources to do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, when you let a specific thing work orders of magnitude better than it should, of course it's going to be a popular tactic.<br /> <br /> If I house ruled the game so that Prime 3 unmaking instantly destroys targets with two successes and ignores the whole damage/soak/health systems, and it inherently coincidental for technology themed mages, of course every Etherite would be using it for their ray guns.. </div> </div> </div>I dont think it is orders of magnitute better than it should; I think it follows RAW. It's simply RAW used in a clever and optimized way. I was looking for alternatives for making low level Spheres used in efficient ways, that came out of my mind. It come be many other things. It could be poisonous fungus, it could be ants just like you suggested, it could be a number of different things. The Octo thing was just a funny style choice, some insanely crazy thing that comically fits with Etherites as &quot;Mad Docs&quot;. Just imagine a roof of the lab of a mad scientist filled with those little yucky things.<br /> <br /> If you wanna be a mad doctor, style is everything.<br /> <br /> That's why I went for the Looney Toones approach instead of boring ants or boring spiders or any such.<br /> <br /> As for their special needs, they have a very special bath of nutrients designed for their needs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Qualitative and subjective aren't the same thing.<br /> <br /> While there's no simple quantitative way to measure complexity in an organism, there are scientifically sound qualitative ways to demonstrate that a squid is more complex than a jelly. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and there's no way I can disagree with you on that, but notice how in this is exactly the root of the problem: you've made a comparison.<br /> &quot;Complexity&quot; cannot be defined, except in a comparative notion. Is a virus complex? Well, compared to a bacteria, absolutely not, even the most &quot;simple&quot; of the archea bacterias are orders of magnitute more complex than any viruses, however if you compare a virus with sand, it is much more complex.<br /> <br /> It's like saying &quot;it's hot/cold today&quot;. Those statements only make sense because we are comparing the temperature of the environment with that of our bodies.<br /> <br /> An AI that reaches singularity, or a God-like alien such as Cthulhu (or a proper God!) could view us as primitives microbes!<br /> <br /> Which is why I said this is a subjective matter.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if I were the player and the ST were to strictly forbid my Octopodus for being &quot;too complex&quot;, I would go for the boring killer spider - or killing Fungus, to keep at least some of my dignity and good name as &quot;Mad Doc&quot;, but the ST would just be crushing my unique style for (subjective) interpretations that would have no impact in the end result (since I would still make &quot;killer-slugs&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T23:29:09-07:00","id":1482577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482568#post1482568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No wonder we Etherites left your decadent organization, and it were the best thing we did!</div> </div> </div> </div>While I understand that you think phrasing this &quot;in character&quot; is humorous, it actually just illustrates the problem with overly &quot;wide&quot; Mage games where players are allowed to completely ignore vital aspects of the game by shouting buzzwords loudly.<br /> <br /> You never actually explain why any of this works from an Etherite paradigm, you just drone on about Science! as a shield from having to justify your decisions.<br /> <br /> You're just sounding like a fanboy for a specific Tradition, and that you let them break the rules if their players can scream Science! loud enough and do some good technobabble. Mage is a game where consequences matter. Etherites might have a specific style (or a few hundred of them really) but there's a cost for living to that style to the extent that you're talking about, and you're saying it should all be ignored.<br /> <br /> Also, I certainly hope you're just being ignorant with implying another poster is a member of the Technocracy with all that entails.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So why arent Cyborgs of the techie boys constantly suffering it? </div> </div> </div>Because it's a much more involved magical process than just mucking around with Life alterations, which results in Permanent Paradox and/or Genetic Flaws as per the Enhancement Background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, I was raising them indeed. It's not like they are difficult to capture in nature. </div> </div> </div>You're talking to someone that's taken care of cuttlefish for an undergrad job to help pay for tuition. You have no idea what the hell you're talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont think it is orders of magnitute better than it should; I think it follows RAW. It's simply RAW used in a clever and optimized way. </div> </div> </div>Except, by the RAW, these things shouldn't last more than 24 hrs with all the alterations you've slap on them resulting in massive Pattern Bleeding. Or, you'd have to go well beyond just Life 2, and end up with them all having a huge pile of Genetic Flaws from all the magical genetic engineering you're doing ala Enhancement. Which means they quickly stop being optimal.<br /> <br /> Hell, you even clearly know this isn't optimal because you call more optimal options boring as an excuse to dismiss them.<br /> <br /> Like the magic rules, and the Etherite style, you're not optimizing you're using the good stuff and just ignoring the complications and downsides because those aren't fun for you apparently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you wanna be a mad doctor, style is everything. </div> </div> </div>And if you want to play Mage RAW, consequences for putting style over other considerations is something you have to deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, and there's no way I can disagree with you on that, but notice how in this is exactly the root of the problem: you've made a comparison. </div> </div> </div><br /> If there's no way you can disagree with me on something, why are you still disagreeing with me on it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway, if I were the player and the ST were to strictly forbid... </div> </div> </div>Stop misrepresenting what I'm saying: &quot;Again, not saying this is impossible, just exceedingly impractical.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T03:43:57-07:00","id":1482584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482577#post1482577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I understand that you think phrasing this &amp;quot;in character&amp;quot; is humorous, it actually just illustrates the problem with overly &amp;quot;wide&amp;quot; Mage games where players are allowed to completely ignore vital aspects of the game by shouting buzzwords loudly.<br /> <br /> You never actually explain why any of this works from an Etherite paradigm, you just drone on about Science! as a shield from having to justify your decisions.<br /> <br /> You're just sounding like a fanboy for a specific Tradition, and that you let them break the rules if their players can scream Science! loud enough and do some good technobabble. Mage is a game where consequences matter. Etherites might have a specific style (or a few hundred of them really) but there's a cost for living to that style to the extent that you're talking about, and you're saying it should all be ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Im guessing that you require your Hermetic players to describe the astrological decans that allow them to use an effect before doing it, right? Whenever a VA wants to use a procedure, do you as your player to write the proper algorithm? Probably you demand your hermetic guy to recite the proper incantation in Enoquian too, to see if they are following the correct synthax of verb non magic and correctly adressing the rules of contagious of proximity, or you ask your Chorist what are the percentages of Earth, Air, Fire and Water they plan to use to do what they wanna do, and so on...<br /> <br /> No. You dont ask any of that, because that's just Paradigm - ie, it's just &quot;mambo jambo&quot;. EVERYTHING in Mage actually is Mambo Jambo - and that includes Science!<br /> <br /> The matter of fact is that in Mage games we can use real life science to better understand how certain ideas might work in the game, but those are NOT real explanations for the things in game. Aka Science is NOT real on Mage games! Science is just another type of Mambo Jambo in this game - perhaps even more than others.<br /> <br /> So yes, when I say that it doesnt matter that they dont have noses, it really doesnt matter. Because this is a Mage game, where everything is a matter of perception and where &quot;Science&quot; is a LIE.<br /> <br /> Sure, gibberish about &quot;tectonic-quantum-transdimensional-babble&quot; is just gibberish techno babble - but what are the Spheres of Prime and Dimensional Science for the techies if not gibberish techno babble?<br /> <br /> And to end it all - it also doesnt matter if they have noses (in an in game &quot;on character&quot; explanation) if those radical transformations require at least 25 successes anyway; so, while the Mad Etherite may believe in whatever &quot;Quantonic&quot; gibberish that he wants to justify this, the game mechanics get it covered by demanding a long procedure with tons of successes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I certainly hope you're just being ignorant with implying another poster is a member of the Technocracy with all that entails. </div> </div> </div>Relax, that was a joke. I use &quot;in character&quot; responses when I want to illustrate Paradigm, and also how we many times use real life logic in a game with different laws from our own. So, when I try to think if A or B would work, I &quot;get in character&quot; rather than trying to find answers irl, be it on sceintific notions or mystic ones. For example, when trying to describe Prime or Dimensional Science, I try to abstract from real life ideas of &quot;soul&quot; or any such, and instead I try to think about what kind of techno babble gibberish would be appropriate. Thus I get &quot;in character&quot; to answer that.<br /> <br /> Besides, what's the problem of being a Technocrat? We are the good guys, you abomination of reality!<br /> <br /> Professor Etherite is just my cover, Im actually agent Smith throught and throught. We are humanity shepards, and we will usher in a New World Order of peace and security!<br /> <br /> Dont worry, you'll learn the truth, OUR truth, after a quick visit to room 101.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it's a much more involved magical process than just mucking around with Life alterations, which results in Permanent Paradox and/or Genetic Flaws as per the Enhancement Background. </div> </div> </div>And why are you assuming that's not the case here?<br /> <br /> Go check the rules about pattern bledding, there they state that it may occur &quot;unless those changes are made permanent&quot;. I knew why that doesnt happen with cyborgs and I knew about permanent paradox. It was a rethorical question.<br /> <br /> You see, Cyborgs dont have Pattern Bleeding because their modifications are permanent; they have Permanent Paradox instead. Which aint a problem when they remain in Mecha Construct because of the local consensus.<br /> <br /> The same applies to my Octopodus; the changes are made permanent, which create either &quot;genetic flaws&quot; (aka Paradox Flaws) or Permanent Paradox.<br /> <br /> None of which matters the least for their purposes <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're talking to someone that's taken care of cuttlefish for an undergrad job to help pay for tuition. You have no idea what the hell you're talking about. </div> </div> </div>Well, Im a marine biologist, so yes, I do have some idea what Im talking about.<br /> <br /> What I am NOT talking about is about you or me trying to use our scubba to put a cephalopodus in a plastic bag to dump it in our homes aquarium and hope to pet it.<br /> <br /> What Im talking about is a hidden conspiracy well funded and infiltrated in scientific communities who also happens to posses unrealistic abilities.<br /> <br /> So, let me rephrase it to make it clear for you: this is trivial for an Etherite (particularly for one with Life 2)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except, by the RAW, these things shouldn't last more than 24 hrs with all the alterations you've slap on them resulting in massive Pattern Bleeding. Or, you'd have to go well beyond just Life 2, and end up with them all having a huge pile of Genetic Flaws from all the magical genetic engineering you're doing ala Enhancement. Which means they quickly stop being optimal. </div> </div> </div>It doesnt matter if they are blind, crazy and prone to be possessed by demons. All that matters is that they do their ONE job.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hell, you even clearly know this isn't optimal because you call more optimal options boring as an excuse to dismiss them. </div> </div> </div>So?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like the magic rules, and the Etherite style, you're not optimizing you're using the good stuff and just ignoring the complications and downsides because those aren't fun for you apparently.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And if you want to play Mage RAW, consequences for putting style over other considerations is something you have to deal with. </div> </div> </div>The consequences in this case are inconsequential. It still follows RAW to the letter, it still works as desired. So, what is the matter to you?<br /> <br /> Also, if I want to stick with the less optimal option, why does it matter to you?<br /> <br /> You seem to be taking this personally, maybe because of your scientific background. But this is a game of fantasy.<br /> <br /> And, up to this point, all that you seem to be implying with is that &quot;it's too hard&quot;. Yeah, but guess what, so it is growing &quot;Homo superiores&quot; on tubes. And yet it is done.<br /> <br /> Unless you can show me the page on M20 that expressily states that my Octopodus are explicitly against RAW, my Etherite will continue to have them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If there's no way you can disagree with me on something, why are you still disagreeing with me on it? </div> </div> </div>Maybe you should read the rest that you chose to ignore<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Stop misrepresenting what I'm saying: &amp;quot;Again, not saying this is impossible, just exceedingly impractical.&amp;quot; </div> </div> </div>So, if is not impossible, why are you still arguing?<br /> <br /> My Mage does 5 &quot;not impossible&quot; things every morning before breakfast!<br /> <br /> You're just bothered with this idea, maybe because it seems too effective to a mere lvl 2 Sphere, I dont know (but if that's the case you should see what Entropy and Mind 2 are capable of).<br /> <br /> It doesnt change the fact that it can be done however. Therefore, it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T06:27:00-07:00","id":1482597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482584#post1482584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. You dont ask any of that, because that's just Paradigm...</div> </div> </div> </div>Your whole argument here is another hyperbolic strawman<br /> <br /> I didn't ask you to do the math, I said your &quot;in character&quot; comments never actually justified how this all works in a Paradigm. Which is, in fact, something I do expect of my players, as the book also expects people to do.<br /> <br /> It also doesn't really help things that you insist on using a misappropriated word from the Mandika people of west Africa used to mock indigenous beliefs by considering them nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yes, when I say that it doesnt matter that they dont have noses, it really doesnt matter. </div> </div> </div>Here's the thing though: it matters because you made it matter by justifying things via scientific concepts. If you magic animals to instinctively attack people with a certain pheromone, you also need to make sure they can sense that pheromone somehow if they're not normally capable of doing so. Again, Mage is a game about consequences. One of the consequences of using scientific knowledge creatively is that you have to account for what you're bringing into the equation. There's a reason why Mage differentiates between mystic and technomagic. Mystics have a harder time incorporating neat science tricks because those aren't part of their paradigms, but also don't have to deal with less fun science facts. Technomages give up some of the freedom mystic mages have to ignore scientific laws so they can exploit those same laws more effectively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Relax, that was a joke. </div> </div> </div>Why should I relax about your bad taste jokes made at my expense?<br /> <br /> If I walked up to you with a hammer, and hit you in the groin so hard your hip broke, would you &quot;relax&quot; and let it slide if I said you should because it's just a joke? I doubt it.<br /> <br /> You generally seem smart enough to know that this is an incredibly stupid thing to say to someone that wasn't amused by your &quot;joke&quot; in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I use &quot;in character&quot; responses when I want to illustrate Paradigm,.... </div> </div> </div>Which has what to do with the actual passage you were responding to? I pointed out that you were just over complicating your &quot;optimal&quot; design, and you busted out an in-character diatribe that didn't address that over complication or even offer up an illustration of the paradigm in question because it moved straight into mocking Technocrats instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, what's the problem of being a Technocrat? </div> </div> </div>They're fascist authoritarians built on a butt load of anti-Semitic tropes about how Jews secretly control the banks, media, and scientific communities in order to control White Christians.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is a conspiracy theorist kitchen sink written by people that forgot how much such conspiracy theories are deeply rooted in the bigotry that lead to millions of people like me being butchered, and is still used to justify violence against us to this day.<br /> <br /> No real person should want to identify with a bigoted stereotype, nor expect other people to feel good about being compared to one. They're not the good guys even if the Traditions aren't great people either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And why are you assuming that's not the case here? </div> </div> </div>1) Just using Life 2.<br /> <br /> 2) Repeated statements that they're meant to be disposable one offs.<br /> <br /> 3) Zero mention of any meaningful flaws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was a rethorical question. </div> </div> </div>No, it was something you were wrong about. Your backtracking and revision is painfully obvious. As is, I hope, your lack of credibility with mean that these things are just &quot;honest mistakes.&quot; Retroactively calling it a rhetorical question is just like the &quot;but it was just a joke&quot; nonsense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The same applies to my Octopodus; the changes are made permanent, which create either &quot;genetic flaws&quot; (aka Paradox Flaws) or Permanent Paradox. </div> </div> </div>Both, if you want to try to be pedantic about this. Biomods, which is what you're describing, suffer from permanent Paradox for any obvious mods they have <b>and</b> one Genetic Flaw per dot in the Enhancement background.<br /> <br /> &quot;The extra Life Sphere damage, then, does not apply to biomods, although the permanent Paradox points still apply to obvious biomods. Like genegineering enhancements, biomods also make the character take one Genetic Flaw per level in the Background Trait.&quot; M20, p. 313.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of which matters the least for their purposes </div> </div> </div>Their stated purpose was Chantry defense optimizing the alterations available with Life 2... having a bunch of Genetic Flaws to have &quot;cool attack squids&quot; instead of &quot;boring ants,&quot; matters because it is a direct refutation that the approach is optimal; which is a claim you directly made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, Im a marine biologist, so yes, I do have some idea what Im talking about. </div> </div> </div>Marine biology is a vast field and the fact that you aren't citing anything more specific than that makes me think you don't have a specialty that directly relates to molluscs let alone cephalopods. You might be a world expert on horseshoe crabs, but that doesn't mean you know more than an undergrad that aced basic zoology when it comes to the rest of the ocean's life. I have met thousands of marine biologists at this point in my life... I don't really care what your specialty is, but every marine biologist I know understands that phrase is uselessly vague for communicating what a scientist does and doesn't have expertise on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What Im talking about is a hidden conspiracy well funded and infiltrated in scientific communities... </div> </div> </div>The Society of Ether is neither as a generality. The ones that really lean into the &quot;mad scientist&quot; bit are especially bad at both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, let me rephrase it to make it clear for you: this is trivial for an Etherite (particularly for one with Life 2) </div> </div> </div>Then I'll restate: nothing in the books supports this conclusion, especially just relying on Life 2 and a Sanctum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesnt matter if they are blind, crazy and prone to be possessed by demons. </div> </div> </div>If Flaws don't matter and aren't enforced, you're not running the RAW or the RAI. You're, even if you don't seem to want to acknowledge it, admitting to my critique: you want the cool good stuff, but want to ignore the consequences that the books say go along with it. If your security squids, or squid ammunition for your squid cannon, pay for all their cool features with being prone to getting possessed by demons, then they're going to get possessed by demons in a fashion that messes with them doing their &quot;one job,&quot; or the Flaw might as well not be there.<br /> <br /> Again, consequences matter. If you ignore the consequences, you're ignoring the whole point of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So? </div> </div> </div>So your statement that they're optimal under the rules seems pretty clearly debunked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The consequences in this case are inconsequential. It still follows RAW to the letter, it still works as desired. So, what is the matter to you? </div> </div> </div>As noted, the consequences being rendered inconsequential by ST fiat is not actually following the RAW to the letter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if I want to stick with the less optimal option, why does it matter to you? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't. But claiming you're suboptimal choices made for the sake of good story are optimal ones is something I have ever right to push back against. Which is what I've been doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You seem to be taking this personally,... </div> </div> </div>You made it personal. Don't deflect your shit on me. You seem very prone to resorting to ad hominem attacks when threads aren't going your way, and then using dirty rhetorical tricks to shift blame onto others. It's grating, I want you to know that I find it grating, because you seem like you have some cool ideas and strong thoughts that I'd like to see more of, instead of having to ignore you because you keeping doing things like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unless you can show me the page on M20 that expressily states that my Octopodus are explicitly against RAW, my Etherite will continue to have them. </div> </div> </div>Until you stat up all of their modifications to know how many points of Genetic Flaws they should have, and then assign them appropriate flaws, they're explicitly against the RAW as I've already cited. Or they all die within 24 hours of magical alteration as you've described at least seven alterations (if not more), which I would then question what traits your Etherite has to be generating and altering them rapidly enough within the RAW to justify having as many of them as you've stated to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe you should read the rest that you chose to ignore. </div> </div> </div>The part where you demonstrate you can't practically demonstrate the difference between qualitative analysis and subjectivity? I didn't ignore it, it didn't merit response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, if is not impossible, why are you still arguing? </div> </div> </div>Is it still unclear from everything above?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My Mage does 5 &quot;not impossible&quot; things every morning before breakfast! </div> </div> </div>Your character is apparently just a dick pic. You keep showing him to people that never asked thinking it's anything other than unpleasant even if they generally enjoy admiring such images on their own terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're just bothered with this idea, maybe because it seems too effective to a mere lvl 2 Sphere, I dont know (but if that's the case you should see what Entropy and Mind 2 are capable of). </div> </div> </div>I'm pointing out all the ways it isn't nearly as effective as you think it is, esp. when there's far more effective options by literally just picking a different animal. I'm not bothered by the idea of a Life mage with guardian animals via a bit of magic. I'm also not impressed by something that I've seen done dozens of times over the last 25 years. I'm not bothered by the idea that an Etherite would do something ridiculous just because it would piss someone like me off.<br /> <br /> What bothers me is trying to ignore the narrative of the game by brushing off, if not full throated endorsement of, hubris. The dark side of the Etherites is that they make these sorts of things to push boundaries, and frequently end up hurting a lot of innocent people, and they think that's justified because in the end they'll make the word a better place and the future Awakened utopia will forgive the evil done to get there. Instead of engaging with the bad side of the Tradition, you're caricaturing them into all flash and no substance because screaming Science! is fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesnt change the fact that it can be done however. Therefore, it is. </div> </div> </div>It is.... what? Pointlessly inefficient? A ludicrous expenditure of effort to do something the Verbena figure out how to do the easy way before the first person inspired by the Kitab al-Alacir Awakened from it? Something that as an experiment will only prove that &quot;obviously prone to horrific results for no noticeable advantage,&quot; was rightfully obvious?<br /> <br /> Because if you think it's more than something like those options, I don't know what more to say to show how off base you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-01-2022, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T10:00:54-07:00","id":1482613,"title":"","content":"Geez. Did I touch a nerve there?<br /> <br /> I wont give myself to answer every point because by the middle of your loooooong text I noticed you're having a mental breakdown. So take a deep breath and calm yourself before continuing.<br /> <br /> I'll just adress a few things from the first half I actually cared to read<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482597#post1482597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I walked up to you with a hammer, and hit you in the groin so hard your hip broke, would you &quot;relax&quot; and let it slide if I said you should because it's just a joke? I doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geez, you're conflating physical violence with words?<br /> <br /> Surely you need to strenght your fragile ego pal. You are too delicate for surviving in this world if you think that a harmless joke is the same as physical castration.<br /> <br /> And you see, I wasnt implying or trying to imply anything. But now I am.<br /> <br /> I guess you're one of &quot;those people&quot; that mommy and daddy told that were special the entire life and now pass out if they hear anything they dont wanna hear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482597#post1482597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're fascist authoritarians built on a butt load of anti-Semitic tropes about how Jews secretly control the banks, media, and scientific communities in order to control White Christians.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Lol no they are not! Hahaha. Dude, you're paranoid. You should seek a doctor.<br /> <br /> First of all, they are based on ideas of the Big Brother, from the book 1984.<br /> <br /> Oh, since you clearly are one of &quot;those people&quot; - aka virtue signalling leftists, since you're making an enormous effort to make it clear, you should know that 1984 was a critic of the socialist Soviet Union. I know you like to scream &quot;fascist&quot; at everything, but you're barking at the wrong three.<br /> <br /> Indeed, they even have the rooms 101 directly from 1984.<br /> <br /> The other source is the movies &quot;Men in Black&quot;, a hidden conspiracy that keeps humanity safe.<br /> <br /> So no, it has nothing to do with &quot;jews controlling everything&quot; which is another type of nonsense that has nothing to do with anything.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;white christians&quot; which I can visualize you typing those words with vitriolic hate, I couldnt give 2 cares since Im an atheist from Brazil. Still, your ideological hate is a sickness of the mind, brother.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482597#post1482597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy is a conspiracy theorist kitchen sink written by people that forgot how much such conspiracy theories are deeply rooted in the bigotry that lead to millions of people like me being butchered, and is still used to justify violence against us to this day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so you're a jew... Geez, it's even worse than I thought.<br /> <br /> Brother... You are DELUDED.<br /> <br /> Do you know what your liberal friends REALLY think about jews?<br /> <br /> Just go check out what the &quot;love&quot; left think about Israel and you'll see where the REAL anti semitism is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482597#post1482597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No real person should want to identify with a bigoted stereotype, nor expect other people to feel good about being compared to one. They're not the good guys even if the Traditions aren't great people either.</div> </div> </div> </div>What? Brother, you're reading too much into it. They have ZERO connections with judaism, jews or any other of the nonsense that certain unsavory people used (and still do) do hurt your people.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know all about the anti-semitic crap around the world, and it's utterly despicable, but you're imagining stuff here. The Technocracy start in Europe by CHRISTIANS, and were evolved by THE BRITISH.<br /> <br /> Like I said, it is based on 1984, MiB but also on the ideas of Illuminatis who were a secret society IN BAVARIA. It has ZERO connection with judaism or the jewish people - and at NO MOMENT I tried to imply ANYTHING other than a fun roleplay moment for a silly game of wizards.<br /> <br /> I am not as fragile to be afraid of words and conflate them with physical violence, nor do I tremble in fear just because you're throwing the victim card to call me &quot;fascist&quot; in a veiled way. I wasnt implying anything before, but now I'll be crystal clear, unlike you and your passive-agressive tantrums: you are paranoid. Period. <br /> <br /> The rest of your nonsense has lost all value given your emotional outburst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T10:16:32-07:00","id":1482615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481989-what-is-your-playstyle-for-mage?p=1482597#post1482597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also doesn't really help things that you insist on using a misappropriated word from the Mandika people of west Africa used to mock indigenous beliefs by considering them nonsense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I almost let this one pass, from the series &quot;Im too fragile for this world&quot; and &quot;words hurt more than bullets&quot; hahahaha.<br /> <br /> Oh, if you &quot;Newspeakers&quot; that want to control the language only knew that you have more in common with the REAL fascists than you have differences...<br /> <br /> One thing that I cannot wrap my head around is: how could a jew be a leftist? Are you this dense?<br /> <br /> Do you not see how the Soviet Union was the closest thing to Nazi Germany that we ever had?<br /> <br /> Can you not see for example how communist China is doing with the Uyghurs what the nazis did to the Jews?<br /> <br /> Brother, the leftist hippies have FAR more in common than they want you to believe. Open your eyes and stop falling to their false rethoric.<br /> <br /> Also... Tell mister sensitivity, what other words are taboo nowadays, even if we have zero clue of the origin? Is calling something as &quot;barbaric&quot; forbidden too nowadays because the romans used it to call non romans in a derrogatory way, is that it? Should I stop using the word &quot;babaric&quot; because some gaul descendant from France might be offended?<br /> <br /> What else has the Thought Police have me do now?<br /> <br /> Do me a favor, go read 1984 and then take a deep look at the mirror. Come talk to me after you've done that deep self analizys.<br /> <br /> Now, your passive-agressive pitful shaming tactic wont work with me. I dont care about the origin of the term &quot;mambo jambo&quot;. I dont care if it has a sad story of the past about it. I like it, and I'll keep using it. Im not going to go into your historical revisionism just to make you feel good about your false &quot;better-than-thou&quot; moralism.<br /> <br /> And I'll certanly NOT engage on Newspeak despicable idiocy. Im a libertarian, freedom for me is non negotiable, and I'll certanly NOT bow down to the angry mob of the REAL fascists - such as yourself. And if you dont think yourself a fascist, again, read 1984 and look at mirror.<br /> <br /> Now have a nice day.<br /> <br /> PS: block me or ban me. I dont care. The message will be received either way, but I wont censor myself on behalf of totalitarians disguised into the &quot;Ministry of Love&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 06-01-2022, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:19:34-07:00","id":1482669,"title":"","content":"Wow, it only took a<i> Day</i> for this thread to get weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T18:48:35-07:00","id":1482697,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">When actual real world anti-semitic conspiracy theories start get equated with Mage, it's time to shut down the thread entirely. Also, accusations of racism and &quot;woke&quot; or &quot;social justice&quot; politics as well.<br /> <br /> Closed.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Take a week off</span> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:imag